---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';
import SourceBadge from '../components/SourceBadge.astro';
import { SITE, GAME_FACTS, IS_RELEASED, LAUNCH_COPY } from '../data/site';

const path = '/download/';
const canonical = new URL(path, SITE.url).href;

const title = 'Beast of Reincarnation Download & PC Requirements';
const description = `Where to download Beast of Reincarnation: official Steam page, ${GAME_FACTS.priceUsd} ${LAUNCH_COPY.purchaseNoun}, day one on Xbox Game Pass, install size and the 45 GB SSD requirement.`;

// 规格数据只用于本页的「at a glance」摘要块。完整 min/rec 对照表已收敛到
// /guides/pc-system-requirements/ 作为唯一正文页，避免三处页面互相稀释同一关键词。
const { minimum, recommended } = GAME_FACTS.systemRequirements;

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: title,
    url: canonical,
    description,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: SITE.url },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Download', item: canonical },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  image="/images/beast-of-reincarnation-koo-shiba-skin.webp"
  imageAlt="Official render of Koo in a brown Shiba coat from Beast of Reincarnation"
>
  <JsonLd slot="head" schema={schema} />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6 text-xs text-ash-400">
      <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
        <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-ember-400">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
        <li class="text-ash-300">Download</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <SourceBadge source="official" />
      <span class="text-xs text-ash-500">Steam listing checked {GAME_FACTS.lastVerified}</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-ash-50 md:text-4xl">
      Beast of Reincarnation Download
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash-300">
      {
        IS_RELEASED ? (
          <>
            <strong class="text-ash-50">Out now.</strong> Beast of Reincarnation released
            {' '}{GAME_FACTS.releaseDate}. You can buy it on an official store or play it through an
            Xbox Game Pass subscription, which has included it since day one — and this page covers
            the official channels, the 45 GB SSD footprint, and the PC requirements you need before
            installing.
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <strong class="text-ash-50">The game is not out yet.</strong> It releases
            {' '}{GAME_FACTS.releaseDate}. Until then the only things you can do are pre-purchase on
            an official store or line up an Xbox Game Pass subscription, which includes it on day one
            — and this page exists so you can check the PC requirements and the
            {' '}45 GB SSD footprint before launch day, not after.
          </>
        )
      }
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-xl border border-ember-800/60 bg-ember-950/25 p-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ember-300">Official PC channel</p>
      <a
        href={GAME_FACTS.source}
        rel="noopener"
        target="_blank"
        class="mt-2 flex items-center gap-4 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ash-50 underline decoration-ember-500/60 underline-offset-4 hover:text-ember-300"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/beast-of-reincarnation-header-banner.webp"
          alt="Beast of Reincarnation Steam store header capsule"
          width="960"
          height="311"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="hidden h-16 w-auto rounded border border-ash-700/60 sm:block"
        />
        <span>Beast of Reincarnation on Steam (App {GAME_FACTS.steamAppId}) →</span>
      </a>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ash-300">
        {GAME_FACTS.priceUsd} standard, {GAME_FACTS.deluxePriceUsd} Deluxe. PlayStation 5 and Xbox
        Series X|S versions are sold on their own platform stores. This site never hosts game files.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-moss-800/60 bg-moss-950/25 p-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-moss-300">
        Subscription channel · Xbox &amp; Windows
      </p>
      <a
        href={GAME_FACTS.gamePass.storeUrl}
        rel="noopener"
        target="_blank"
        class="mt-2 inline-block font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ash-50 underline decoration-moss-500/60 underline-offset-4 hover:text-moss-300"
      >
        Day one on Xbox Game Pass Ultimate &amp; PC Game Pass →
      </a>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ash-300">
        If you subscribe, you do not have to buy the game: it enters the catalogue on
        {' '}{GAME_FACTS.releaseDate}, the same day it goes on sale. It is also an
        {' '}<strong class="text-ash-100">Xbox Play Anywhere</strong> title, so one entitlement covers
        Xbox console and Windows PC, and it is flagged
        {' '}<strong class="text-ash-100">Handheld optimized</strong>. Game Pass does not cover the
        Steam or PlayStation versions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Downloading it through Xbox Game Pass</h2>
      <p>
        On Xbox and Windows there is a second route that does not involve buying the game.
        {' '}<strong>Beast of Reincarnation is in the Game Pass catalogue from day one.</strong> The
        Xbox Wire Developer_Direct post states it "will be available with Xbox Game Pass Ultimate on
        day one, and is an Xbox Play Anywhere and Handheld Optimized title", and the
        {' '}<a href={GAME_FACTS.gamePass.storeUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">official Xbox game
        page</a> repeats the same thing as "Play day one with Game Pass · Available August 4, 2026".
        Microsoft's store entitlement data for product {GAME_FACTS.gamePass.productId} lists two
        subscriptions: Xbox Game Pass (console) and PC Game Pass.
      </p>
      <p>
        Practical consequences for download planning:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Xbox Play Anywhere</strong> — one entitlement, whether bought or subscribed, covers
          Xbox Series X|S and Windows. You install on both without paying twice, and saves sync.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Handheld optimized</strong> — Microsoft has verified it against supported Windows
          handhelds, so the 45 GB SSD figure matters there too, on a device where free space is
          usually tighter.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Xbox Cloud</strong> — the Developer_Direct post lists Xbox Cloud alongside console
          and PC, which means Ultimate subscribers have a streaming option with no download at all.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>It does not extend to Steam or PlayStation.</strong> There is no subscription route
          on either. If you want it on Steam, you buy it.
        </li>
        <li>
          A subscription is not ownership. Access lasts while the game stays in the catalogue, and
          nothing has been said about how long that will be.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Is there a demo to download right now?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>No.</strong> {GAME_FACTS.developer} and {GAME_FACTS.publisher} never announced a
        demo, a beta, or a public test build, and none appeared at launch. The "demo" you may have
        read about in pre-release coverage was a press event — journalists played a timed hands-on
        build at a Game Freak showcase, not something that was ever downloadable. The full game is
        the only build there has ever been.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is worth stating plainly, because "beast of reincarnation demo" and "download" are
        exactly the queries that fake-installer and repack sites farm. If a page offers you a
        {' '}<em>free</em> download, a cracked installer, or a mobile APK, it is not giving you this
        game. The Steam link above, App {GAME_FACTS.steamAppId}, is the only PC address worth
        trusting{IS_RELEASED ? '' : ', and there is nothing to distribute yet'}.
      </p>

      <h2>How buying and downloading works</h2>
      {
        IS_RELEASED ? (
          <ol>
            <li>Buy on Steam and the download starts straight away — the build is unlocked.</li>
            <li>
              The unlock happened at 00:00 UTC on {GAME_FACTS.releaseDate}, the same instant in every
              region. See the <a href="/release-date/">release date page</a> for why some Steam
              regions displayed the previous day.
            </li>
            <li>
              On Xbox and Windows a Game Pass subscription installs it the same way, with no purchase.
            </li>
          </ol>
        ) : (
          <ol>
            <li>Pre-purchase on Steam and the game appears in your library as unreleased.</li>
            <li>
              Steam may enable a <strong>preload</strong> shortly before launch so files are on disk
              in advance. Publishers opt into that individually and {GAME_FACTS.publisher} has not
              confirmed whether they will.
            </li>
            <li>
              On {GAME_FACTS.releaseDate} the build unlocks at 00:00 UTC — the same instant in every
              region. See the <a href="/release-date/">release date page</a> for why some Steam
              regions display the previous day.
            </li>
          </ol>
        )
      }

      <h2>Install size and drive requirements</h2>
      <p>
        Steam lists <strong>45 GB of available space</strong>, and an <strong>SSD is required</strong>
        {' '}— not recommended, required. Plan for more than 45 GB free: Steam needs headroom while it
        unpacks, and the launch build is already at version {GAME_FACTS.launchVersion}, so patches
        have added to the footprint. If your only free space is on a mechanical drive, sort that out
        before you start the download rather than halfway through it.
      </p>

      <h2>PC system requirements at a glance</h2>
      <p>
        The short version, from the official Steam listing: you need a
        {' '}<strong>{minimum.gpu.split(' or ')[0]}</strong> class GPU at minimum, 16 GB RAM at both
        tiers, and 45 GB on an SSD. One detail matters more than the part numbers — both tiers quote
        1080p <em>with upscaling in Performance mode</em>, so the 40fps and 60fps figures are already
        upscaled, not native.
      </p>
      <div class="not-prose my-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/40 p-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ash-500">Minimum</p>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ash-200">{minimum.gpu}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ash-500">{minimum.notes}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-ash-800 bg-ash-900/40 p-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ash-500">Recommended</p>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ash-200">{recommended.gpu}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ash-500">{recommended.notes}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Full CPU, OS, DirectX and storage rows for both tiers — plus why the minimum note names DLSS
        alongside a GTX 1070 that cannot run it — are on our
        {' '}<a href="/guides/pc-system-requirements/"><strong>PC system requirements page</strong></a>.
        That page is the one we keep current against the store listing.
      </p>

      <h2>What ships in the box</h2>
      <p>
        Steam confirms the following for the PC version: {GAME_FACTS.features.join(', ')}. Language
        support is {GAME_FACTS.languages}.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Deluxe edition is listed at {GAME_FACTS.deluxePriceUsd}, and its contents are now
        itemised on the official pre-order post. On top of the standard pre-order bonus, Deluxe adds
        an <strong>Alternate Black Shiba Skin for Koo</strong>, a <strong>Big Dipper sword for
        Emma</strong>, an <strong>Oni's Hat for Emma</strong>, a larger <strong>100,000 Amber</strong>
        {' '}grant (the standard edition gives 30,000), and <strong>Vegetable Seedlings</strong> for
        in-game use.
      </p>
      <p>
        The pre-order bonus itself: both editions grant an <strong>Alternate Brown Shiba Skin for
        Koo</strong> plus Amber (30,000 standard, 100,000 with Deluxe). That wording comes from the
        official Steam pre-order announcement and the console storefronts.
      </p>

      <figure>
        <img
          src="/images/beast-of-reincarnation-koo-shiba-skin.webp"
          alt="Official Beast of Reincarnation render of Koo in a tan brown Shiba coat with golden blighted foliage along his back and tail"
          width="1600"
          height="900"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="rounded-xl border border-ash-800"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Koo in a brown Shiba coat, from the official store gallery. The pre-order bonus listed on
          both console stores is a Brown Shiba Skin for Koo plus 30,000 Amber.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Console downloads</h2>
      <p>
        The PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S versions released the same day and are downloaded
        through their own storefronts — on Xbox, either as a purchase or through Game Pass. No
        Nintendo version has been announced. Install sizes for the console builds have not been
        published; the 45 GB figure above is the PC requirement.
      </p>

      <h2>Before you start playing</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Confirm at least 50–60 GB free on an SSD.</li>
        <li>Update GPU drivers — both tiers assume upscaling, so driver-side scaling matters.</li>
        <li>Check your GPU against the table above and decide your upscaling setting in advance.</li>
        <li>
          If you want English voice acting, set it from the <strong>main menu</strong> before starting
          a save — the in-game options do not expose the audio language.
        </li>
        <li>
          Read the <a href="/game-info/">confirmed game info</a> so you know which systems are real
          and which are still unannounced.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Then start with our <a href="/guides/launch-day-beginner-guide/">beginner's guide</a>, which
        covers the parry, florescence points and bloom arts as they work in the shipped build, or the
        {' '}<a href="/guides/nushi-boss-fight/">Rangifer Nushi fight</a>. Pages written before launch
        that we have not yet rewritten still carry a notice saying so.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a
        href="/release-date/"
        class="rounded-lg bg-ember-600 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-ash-950 transition-colors hover:bg-ember-500"
      >
        Release date & platforms
      </a>
      <a
        href="/game-info/"
        class="rounded-lg border border-ash-600 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-ash-100 transition-colors hover:border-ash-400 hover:bg-ash-800"
      >
        Confirmed game info
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
